====================================================================================================
(B) IS THE JITTER BOUND THE RIGHT SHAPE?  (my marked spot, pressed harder)
    Writing the derivation out properly SHARPENS it: the jitter is eps = m_j beta with
    m_j <= 2v, and the progression step is eta = 2 v beta, so *** eps <= eta exactly ***.
    The per-class error is then at most eps.V/eta <= V <= 2M(L+1) -- the same shape as
    error (i), not a separate mechanism -- giving 4qM/N + 4M/(Q+1) in the mean, which is
    HALF what r113 claimed.  The paper's bound is therefore valid and generous.
    What must still be true: the jitter vanishes at beta = 0 and grows with |beta|.
====================================================================================================
