          0.125     0.2511   3.573e-04           0.079753
          0.250     0.5022   2.486e-04           0.095759
          0.500     1.0044   8.086e-07           0.127771
          1.000     2.0087   0.000e+00           0.191796
    The measured jitter vanishes at beta = 0 and grows with |beta|, inside a bound that
    also grows with |beta| -- consistent.  It is not linear in beta: the difference of
    two oscillating sums is not a smooth function of beta, and the bound is two orders
    of magnitude loose, so the growth rate carries no information beyond its sign.

