(C) ADVERSARIAL SEARCH.  Not a uniform net: hunt directly for a minor theta where the
    weighted mean falls below (1/2) log 2, using the structure of the claim against it
    (near-rational points with small v, and the worst beta inside each box).
====================================================================================================
    adversarial minimum over 178 moduli x all numerators x 9 offsets:
      G = 0.346574 at (q,a,beta/box,theta) = (4, 1, np.float64(0.0), np.float64(0.25))
      (1/2) log 2 = 0.346574     shortfall = -1.110e-16
    no minor theta beats the floor

====================================================================================================
(D) END-TO-END ON REAL INSTANCES.  Draw A from the Cramer model, compute
    max over minor theta of F_A(theta)^(1/b), and ask whether the excess over 1/sqrt2
    is BOUNDED (a constant factor, as rem:notmax says) or GEOMETRIC (theorem false).
====================================================================================================
    *** THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS TEST WAS BROKEN, AND ITS CONTROL DID NOT NOTICE. ***
    A uniform net of 30001 points has spacing 1.7e-5 while the peak at theta = 1/4 is
    O(1/N) = 7.8e-6 wide at N = 128001, so the scan stepped over it and reported a
    MAXIMUM of 0.5690 -- below a value it had itself evaluated.  The control passed
    anyway, because it checked F_A(1/4) rather than checking that THE SEARCH FINDS 1/4.
    F55 says a search needs a positive control; the control must be on the search.
    Repaired: the peaks live at rationals, so evaluate at every a/q with q <= 20 and
    sweep +-5/N around each, and gate the row on the search recovering theta = 1/4.
          N      b  max F^(1/b)   - 1/sqrt2  b log(sqrt2 max)    argmax  control
       2001    322     0.707107   1.221e-15            0.0000   0.25000     True
       8001   1024     0.707107   1.887e-15            0.0000   0.25000     True
      32001   3496     0.707107   2.465e-14            0.0000   0.75000     True
     128001  11804     0.707107  -1.077e-14           -0.0000   0.25000     True
    CONTROL, correctly placed this time: the search must LOCATE theta = 1/4 and return
    1/sqrt2 there.  A False invalidates the row rather than refuting the theorem.
    The theorem predicts the last column stays O(1) while b grows; a column growing
    linearly in b would mean a geometric excess and would refute thm:rate.
    SCOPE OF THIS ROW (F01): it shows the maximum does not EXCEED 1/sqrt2 geometrically.
    It does not reproduce the O(1/b) excess of rem:notmax, whose optimal offset is of
    order 1/(N sqrt b) and finer than this grid; that remains measured in mq4_r107.

====================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  (A) three error terms inside their bounds : YES
  (C) adversarial search found no breach    : YES
  (D) read the last column: O(1) supports thm:rate, linear-in-b refutes it.
  This is a self-audit.  It cannot replace the independent read by the other model,
  and the report says so.
